# The Vercel deploy builds the landing and the web app (`npm run site:build` → web/dist)
# plus the serverless functions in api/. Everything the mobile and desktop targets need is dead
# weight in the upload, and the CLI does NOT fall back to .gitignore here: without this
# file the deploy ships 41k files and fails the 15k limit outright.
#
# What the build actually reads: web/, src/ (aliased as @staysound), sites/landing/, api/, package.json,
# package-lock.json, vercel.json, tsconfig.json.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, this file uses .gitignore
# matching, so a bare `components/` would also swallow web/src/components/ and break the
# build.

# Rust desktop app — target/ alone is ~22k files
/src-tauri/

# Native mobile projects and modules
/android/
/ios/
/modules/
/macos-native/
/plugins/
/patches/

# Expo/React Native app shell, unused by the web build
/app/
/components/
/constants/
/assets/

# Build output, media renders and scratch
/out/
# The landing is part of the site (scripts/build-site.mjs); only its sources are needed.
/sites/admin/
/sites/landing/node_modules/
/sites/landing/.next/
/sites/landing/out/
/remotion/
/docs/
/update/
/.audit/
/tmp_*
/design-qa*
*.apk
*.dmg
*.mp4
*.mp3

# Tooling state
/.expo/
/.impeccable/
/.desktop-sidecar/
/.venv-demucs/
